"notes": [
    "GET /api/v1/user returns the account id, email and the account's own personal token in a top-level token field. Only /id and /email are selected, so that token never reaches a task, review or result.",
    "GET /api/v1/tasks returns results plus an optional next_cursor; the profile reads at most three cursor pages.",
    "POST /api/v1/tasks requires content. description, project_id, section_id, labels, due dates and priority are optional, so the reviewed profile sends content and description only and an omitted project_id targets the Inbox.",
    "GET /api/v1/tasks/{task_id} documents description on the task object. read_task stays minimal so a task without one still reads, and read_task_detail returns it for a task that documents it.",
    "GET /api/v1/projects and GET /api/v1/projects/{project_id} document results with a next_cursor and a project object. The documented project response is a union of the personal and workspace views, so only the fields present in both are selected; workspace-only access, role and inbox_project fields are deliberately not selected."
  ],
